Issues Encountered
Memory, Stack, and Queue components share the same data-memory space, so their RAM address ranges had to be kept separate.
Several Week 3 features required changes to shared CPU and UI files, requiring coordination between team members.
Queue pointer updates and circular wrap-around required additional testing to ensure correct FIFO behavior.
The increasing number of CPU instructions required corresponding updates to instruction decoding and execution.

Decisions Made
Use separate RAM regions for Stack and Queue storage to prevent conflicts.
Use the existing data memory for both Stack and Queue storage.
Implement the Queue as a fixed-size circular FIFO buffer.
Use HEAD, TAIL, and COUNT values to track queue state.
Keep queue operations based on existing instructions rather than introducing additional queue-specific opcodes.
Continue using the existing CPU Fetch → Decode → Execute structure.

